---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Log1Content from "../../components/Log1Content.astro";
import "../../styles/logs.css";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="LLVM vs. GraalVM — Oreslang engineering log #1"
  description="Alex Mills compares missing Oreslang features, LLVM and GraalVM runtime strengths, true guest-code AOT, optional JIT, and a shared compiler architecture."
>
  <nav class="log-breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><a href="/logs/">Logs</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span aria-current="page">#1</span></nav>
  <header class="log-entry-header">
    <p class="kicker">Engineering log / 001</p>
    <details class="log-prompt-disclosure">
      <summary class="log-prompt-summary">
        <h1 class="log-prompt-heading">
          <span class="log-prompt-topline">
            <span class="log-prompt-word">prompt</span>
            <span class="log-prompt-toggle" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          </span>
          <span class="log-prompt-glimmer" aria-hidden="true">are there any features of oreslang that we don't have yet that we should? which features could be in llvm but shouldn't be in graal/jvm? which features should be in graal/jvm but not in llvm? we want it to be aot-compiled in both (with opt-in or opt-out jit optimizations)</span>
          <span class="log-prompt-cue" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </h1>
      </summary>
      <div class="log-prompt-reveal">
        <p class="log-prompt-reveal-label">The original question</p>
        <p class="log-prompt-full-text">are there any features of oreslang that we don't have yet that we should? which features could be in llvm but shouldn't be in graal/jvm? which features should be in graal/jvm but not in llvm? we want it to be aot-compiled in both (with opt-in or opt-out jit optimizations)</p>
      </div>
    </details>
    <div class="log-entry-meta"><span>Authored by <strong>Alex Mills</strong></span><span aria-hidden="true">·</span><time datetime="2026-10-08T21:04:00Z">October 8, 2026 · 21:04 UTC</time></div>
    <p class="log-entry-intro">One language, two production AOT backends, and a deliberate choice about what belongs in LLVM versus GraalVM.</p>
  </header>
  <div class="log-entry-layout">
    <aside class="log-toc" aria-label="On this page">
      <p class="eyebrow">In this entry</p>
      <ol>
        <li><a href="#missing-features">Missing features</a></li>
        <li><a href="#llvm-native-features">LLVM-native capabilities</a></li>
        <li><a href="#graal-jvm-features">Graal/JVM integration</a></li>
        <li><a href="#aot-jit-modes">AOT and JIT modes</a></li>
        <li><a href="#shared-compiler-architecture">Shared compiler IR</a></li>
        <li><a href="#implementation-order">Implementation order</a></li>
      </ol>
    </aside>
    <article class="log-article prose" aria-label="Engineering log #1"><Log1Content /></article>
  </div>
  <nav class="log-entry-footer" aria-label="Article navigation"><a href="/logs/">← All engineering logs</a><a href="https://github.com/ores-truffle-oreslang/oreslang-source.llvm">LLVM compiler source ↗</a></nav>
</BaseLayout>
